.TITLE "scp"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Copies files securely between hosts. It uses __SSH__ for data transfer and authentication, providing a secure way to move files across a network.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**scp file user@host:path**
Copies a local file to a specified path on a remote host.
> __file__ local path | __user@host:path__ remote destination

**scp user@host:path local_path**
Copies a remote file to a specified local directory.
> __user@host:path__ remote source | __local_path__ local destination

**scp -r folder user@host:path**
Copies an entire directory recursively to a remote host.
> __-r__ recursive flag

**scp -P 2222 file user@host:path**
Uses a specific port to connect to the remote host.
> __-P__ port flag | __2222__ port number

.DIV "SUMMARY"
While __scp__ is convenient for simple file transfers, the __rsync__ command is often preferred for large or complex transfers as it supports resuming interrupted tasks and delta-encoding.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ssh** **mac:rsync**

